WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.762
Here's what Microsoft gives you.

2
00:00:01.762 --> 00:00:06.774
Learn's audit history page shows PIM's own
audit view, says it covers thirty days,

3
00:00:06.774 --> 00:00:11.555
and gives three sample queries: one for
role activations, one that follows a

4
00:00:11.555 --> 00:00:16.875
single request, and one that follows a
whole cycle from activation to deactivation.

5
00:00:16.875 --> 00:00:19.964
Learn's activity list
names every event PIM logs,

6
00:00:19.964 --> 00:00:23.362
and its security operations
guide says what to watch.

7
00:00:23.362 --> 00:00:27.791
The queries only exist in the web
page, so the repository pins it,

8
00:00:27.791 --> 00:00:32.900
unmodified, and the tests run all three
over a set of fictional audit rows.

9
00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:35.110
It's a test, not a query engine.
